-- title:
--   Level automorphisms: transitive on the q+1 ends, no fixed smooth place (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Places are taken in the sense of the project's [`AlgebraicCurve.Place K F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22): a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself, whose ring is a principal ideal ring, with `ord` the associated normalised integer valuation, `IsRational` meaning that $K$ surjects onto the residue field, and `evalAt` the resulting $K$-valued evaluation (zero outside the valuation subring).
--
--   The base data at level $M'$ are: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) over $\kappa$, subject to `hW`, which says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. of those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` in `ssJSet q κ`; an inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field) into `fieldBar q M'` (the analogous base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups given by `dvd_sq_mul q M'`); a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with reduced field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers` together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A \to \kappa$ on constants, normalising functions by constants, and carrying places to places of the reduced field in a degree-preserving way compatible with divisors of functions; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that $R_0$ is coefficientwise reduction: every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` belongs to `R₀.integers`, and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a member of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   The data above the special fibre are: a field $FSS$ that is an algebra over $\kappa$; a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to `fieldBar q M'` with reduced field $FSS$ (a valuation subring `R.integers` with surjective residue map onto $FSS$, kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A \to \kappa$ on constants, and with every nonzero function normalisable by a constant to have nonzero residue); a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$; and, indexed by the places $Q$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, a subring $S_Q \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q : A[T] \to S_Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_{0,Q} : S_Q \to \kappa$, and a set $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are the following. `h0`: $FSS$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$. `h1` ($R$ lies over $s$): for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `hle` lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue is the image under $\kappa \to FSS$ of `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $f$. `h2` (level invariance): for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the preimage of `R.integers` under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is `R.integers`. `hcard`: $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   `hpkg` (the smooth-point package; thirteen clauses, summarised here) requires, for every place $Q \notin N$: that $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$; that $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; that $\varphi_Q$ sends constants $C\,a$ to the images of $a \in A$ and that $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$, while $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(T)) = 0$; that for every $c \in A$ with residue $0$ there is a unique $A$-valued ring homomorphism on $S_Q$ restoring $a$ on $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$, reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$, and sending $\varphi_Q(T)$ to $c$; that every $f \in S_Q$ lies in `R.integers` with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, the residue of that element in the residue field of $Q$ being the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$; that the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(T)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; that $D_Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` at which all $f \in S_Q$ are regular with `P.evalAt f` in $A$, and for which $A$-valuation of `P.evalAt f` is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_{0,Q}(f)=0$; that every $A$-valued section of $S_Q$ over $A$ reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ is `evalAt` of a unique $P \in D_Q$; that for $P \in D_Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_Q$ and `P.evalAt h` $\ne 0$; that a nonzero function of order $0$ at every $P \in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and that a function in `R.integers` regular at every $P \in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   `hdisj`: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, if some place belongs to both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ then $Q = Q'$. `hcusp`: for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the order at $P$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the coefficientwise image of `jq` is nonnegative. `heqv`: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, for every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, and for every place $Q$ of $FSS$: the place `R.resAut τ _ • Q` lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and if $Q \notin N$ then `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (Dx Q)`, i.e. $\{P : \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_Q\}$, equals $D_{\mathtt{R.resAut}\,\tau\,\cdot\,Q}$; here `R.resAut τ` is the $\kappa$-algebra automorphism of $FSS$ induced by $\tau$ on the reduced field.
--
--   The final hypothesis `hdl` (the level-equivariant Drinfeld identification) assumes: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and an isomorphism $e$ of $\kappa$-algebras from $FSS$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the action of $C_s$) such that the cardinality of $C_s$ equals `placeWidthChar q M' s`, which is `jWidthChar q (s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M'))` divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`, and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every proof that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and every proof that $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the automorphism of $FSS$ induced by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` corresponds under $e$ to the action [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) of $(\mathtt{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is a conjunction of two assertions. First, the level automorphisms act transitively on $N$: for all places $x, x'$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ lying in $N$, there exist $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a proof that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` preserves `R.integers` such that the induced automorphism `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ)` carries $x$ to $x'$. Second, no place outside $N$ is fixed by all of them: for every place $Q \notin N$ there exist $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a proof that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` preserves `R.integers` such that `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ) • Q ≠ Q`.
--
--   This is the case $q = 2$, at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the statement that on a supersingular component of the special fibre at $q$ of the curve of level $q^2M'$ — identified via the Drinfeld curve with a quotient of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}(\mathrm{DL})$ — the level automorphisms permute the $q+1$ ends transitively and fix no smooth place. It is used in the subsequent analysis of level orbits and inertia generators on the Drinfeld quotient.
